Uses binary search to find the minimum in a rotated sorted array.
Compares nums[mid] with nums[right] to decide which half contains the minimum.

If nums[mid] < nums[right] → search left half
Else → search right half

Stops when left == right, which is the minimum.
Time Complexity: O(log n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
class Solution {
    public int findMin(int[] nums) {
        int left=0, right=nums.length-1;
        while(left<right){
            int mid=left+(right-left)/2;
            if(nums[mid]<nums[right]){
                right=mid;
            }else{
                left=mid+1;
            }
        }
        return nums[left];
        
    }
}
